      "name": {
        "name": "Poly(R)-hydroxyalkanoic acid synthase, class II",
        "short": "PHA_synth_II"
      },
      "description": [
        {
          "text": "<p>This entry represents the class II subfamily of poly(R)-hydroxyalkanoate synthases, which polymerises hydroxyacyl-CoAs, typically with six to fourteen carbons in the hydroxyacyl backbone into aliphatic esters termed poly(R)-hydroxyalkanoic acids [[cite:PUB00013497]]. These polymers accumulate as carbon and energy storage inclusions in many species and can amount to 90 percent of the dry weight of cell.</p>",
