      "name": {
        "name": "Poly(3-hydroxyalkanoate) depolymerase",
        "short": "PHA_depoly_arom"
      },
      "description": [
        {
          "text": "<p>This family consists of the polyhydroxyalkanoic acid (PHA) depolymerase of Pseudomonas oleovorans and related species. This enzyme is part of polyester storage and mobilisation system as in many bacteria. However, species containing this enzyme are unusual in their capacity to produce aromatic polyesters when grown on carbon sources such as benzoic acid or phenylacetic acid [[cite:PUB00015514]].</p>",
